      "label": "top text overlay",
      "description": "what's the difference between a jew and a pizza?",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_93e8b785",
      "@type": "VisualMaterial",
      "instance_name": "Jewish_man",
      "label": "person",
      "description": "A middle-aged man wearing a black suit, white shirt, black tie, and a kippah (yarmulke) on his head, with a tallit (prayer shawl) draped over his shoulders. He is seated in wooden pews, smiling at the camera. His attire and setting suggest he is in a synagogue or Jewish place of worship. This is the central human subject of the image.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9cdf5f47",
      "@type": "Scene",
      "instance_name": "jew_and_pizza_scene",
      "label": "Jewish man and pizza in a synagogue setting",
      "description": "The scene depicts a Jewish man seated in wooden pews in what appears to be a synagogue, juxtaposed with a large pepperoni pizza and pizza-making ingredients (tomatoes, sauce, cutting board, knife) arranged on a wooden table above him. The scene is framed by text that poses a hateful question and delivers a violent antisemitic punchline, creating a composition that equates the man with a pizza in a context of historical persecution. The spatial arrangement places the man in the foreground (lower half) and the pizza in the background (upper half), visually linking them through the meme's text.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a8132fb8",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "antisemitic_stereotype_jew_screaming_in_oven",
      "label": "Antisemitic Stereotype: Jew Screaming in the Oven",
      "description": "This is a deeply offensive and historically rooted antisemitic trope that equates Jewish people with inanimate objects, specifically implying that Jews are 'screaming' or suffering when subjected to persecution, particularly during the Holocaust. The meme uses the punchline 'a pizza doesn't scream when you put it in the oven' to mock Jewish religious practice and identity, invoking this harmful stereotype. This trope is a direct reference to the Holocaust and the dehumanization of Jewish victims.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9fe62fb3",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "holocaust_persecution",
      "label": "Historical Event: Holocaust Persecution",
      "description": "The Holocaust was the systematic, state-sponsored persecution and murder of six million Jews by Nazi Germany and its collaborators during World War II. The antisemitic stereotype referenced in the meme is directly tied to this historical atrocity, where Jews were dehumanized and subjected to genocide. The meme's punchline is a crude, violent analogy that mocks this historical trauma.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a4549d82",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "antisemitic_stereotype_mocking_religious_practice",
      "label": "Antisemitic Stereotype: Mocking Religious Practice",
      "description": "This stereotype involves portraying Jewish religious practices, such as wearing a kippah or using a tallit, as absurd or comical, often to demean Jewish identity. The meme visually juxtaposes a Jewish man in religious attire with a pizza, using this contrast to mock his faith and cultural identity, which is a form of religious discrimination.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_540c339c",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "antisemitic_stereotype_jew_as_inanimate_object",
      "label": "Antisemitic Stereotype: Jew as Inanimate Object",
      "description": "This is a dehumanizing antisemitic trope that reduces Jewish people to objects or animals, stripping them of their humanity. The meme equates the Jewish man with a pizza, an inanimate object, to imply he is not a real person but a thing that can be 'cooked' or destroyed without consequence, which is a direct reference to the Holocaust.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_34486072",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "hateful_laughter",
      "label": "hateful and mocking laughter",
      "description": "The Jewish man is smiling, which in the context of the meme is not an expression of genuine happiness but is used to convey a mocking, cruel, and hateful tone. The smile is juxtaposed with the antisemitic punchline, suggesting a sinister or derisive amusement at the suffering of Jewish people, particularly in reference to the Holocaust. This is not a natural expression but a performative one meant to mock and dehumanize.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0deecc02",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "jew_pizza_analogical_mapping",
      "label": "Jew is mapped onto Pizza",
      "description": "The textual question 'what's the difference between a Jew and a pizza?' and the punchline 'a pizza doesn't scream when you put it in the oven' create an analogical mapping where the Jewish man (visual entity) is equated with a pizza (visual entity). This mapping is explicitly stated in the text and reinforced by the visual juxtaposition of the man and the pizza. The mapping is hateful and antisemitic, reducing the Jewish man to an inanimate object, specifically invoking the historical antisemitic trope of the 'Jew as screaming in the oven' during the Holocaust.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e6af880f",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the antisemitic stereotype of the Jew as an inanimate object",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the hateful analogical mapping where the Jewish man (VisualMaterial: Jewish_man) is equated with a pizza (VisualMaterial: pizza), as explicitly stated in the textual material (TextualMaterial: top_text) and reinforced by the scene (Scene: jew_and_pizza_scene). The punchline 'a pizza doesn't scream when you put it in the oven' directly invokes the antisemitic trope of the 'Jew screaming in the oven' during the Holocaust, which dehumanizes Jewish people by reducing them to an object. The user, by consuming and engaging with this meme, is implicitly projected onto this dehumanizing and violent stereotype.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3aa59fed",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Hateful",
      "description": "The meme directly equates a Jewish man with a pizza and references the antisemitic trope of Jews screaming in the oven during the Holocaust, which is a hateful attack on Jewish identity and a dehumanizing stereotype.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7710fcf5",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience is individuals who are familiar with or may be exposed to antisemitic stereotypes, particularly those who understand the historical reference to the Holocaust and the trope of the 'Jew screaming in the oven.' The meme is designed to provoke a reaction from people who either find the stereotype humorous or are unaware of its deeply offensive and hateful nature, thereby reinforcing or spreading antisemitic content. The audience may include those who engage with internet memes that rely on crude, violent, and dehumanizing analogies, often without recognizing the historical trauma they invoke.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d6e9d85c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
  ]
